{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465564-in-setting-vampire-texts-and-the-general-public","id":1465564,"title":"in-setting vampire texts and the general public","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-27T14:02:34-07:00","id":1465564,"title":"in-setting vampire texts and the general public","content":"What vampire texts should be known to the public in the setting of VtM? By that I mean not only do vampires know about it, but ordinary mortals in the setting also know about it. It might be popularly known, known only to the academic community (scholars, museums, and such), or among specialized audience (like the occult community, Egyptologists, archaeologists, conspiracy theorists, horror literature aficionados, etc.). For our purposes, this means more than just the Arcanum or Inquisition and the like. It's out there for people who may not know or believe vampires exist, but still encounter the text.<br /> <br /> For example, both the Book of Nod and Revelations of the Dark Mother (a version of the Lilith Cycle) are supposed to have been released to the general population. If I remember correctly, the English translation vampire author of the Book of Nod intended his book to only be for vampires, but somehow entered general circulation; and the Revelations was intentionally meant as a Masquerade breaching non-fiction book. Of course, the epistolary novel Dracula was meant in the VtM setting to also be a non-fiction expose of vampires, but was mistakenly thought to be fiction.<br /> <br /> There's been a lot of fictional texts over the years in the game, but it's not always clear whether it should be limited to just vampires knowing about them, or if any are known to mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T17:07:26-07:00","id":1465578,"title":"","content":"I think unless there is a successful effort in tracking down and securing every single copy of a book, you can bet there's a huge chance a given text went public. And there are others, as the opening letters from 1st and 2nd cores, very recent and very thorough expositions on the Kindred.<br /> <br /> Dracula puts a complex twist to it. It exposes a lot about the Kindred, but also hides a lot, as contrary to common belief a lot of the modern image of vampires that informed VtM is a posterior development, and Dracula itself isn't really the first novel to do it, being preceded (and inspired) by <i>The Vampyre</i>, by Polidori.<br /> <br /> Going for the literary expositions, <i>The Vampyre</i> reveals the existence of the Kindred and a few core characteristics. <i>Dracula</i> reveals many more traits and common Disciplines, but also mix them with several falsehoods. <i>Nosferatu</i> reveals the weakness to the sun, kept a secret until then. And Anne Rice's <i>Vampire Chronicles</i> reveal a ton of information, either directly or by straight opposition, almost every detail not yet covered, including Humanity, Wassail, Disciplines and so much more.<br /> <br /> Of interest is also what could be inferred of their creation with we cross the RL origins of those stories with VtM's implications. <i>The Vampyre</i> is based on Lord Byron to a great extend, so maybe Byron was a Revenant that found it amusing to tell that little bit just to see where it goes. The mystery is how Byron got to be nicknamed after Lambach. <i>Dracula</i>, contrary to popular belief, was not based on the rl Vlad &quot;Dracula&quot; Tepes III, but since in VtM they're one and the same, it could be based on Stoker's hearing about him either from himself or Lambach. Anne Rice especially must be protected by someone really powerful, as she kept releasing secrets about the Kindred for many years, actually still does to this day.<br /> <br /> But all said and done, it is hard to tell what the effects are in the public. Without records of any original fragments to give it academic credentials, <i>The Book of Nod</i> is left weightless, the same goes for the <i>Revelations</i>. Saying that your weird book is non-fiction don't really get you much farther than the usual nutjobs that would believe it even if you said it was fiction. The market is choke-full of books about vampires, each with its own version of them, and without knowledge of actual Kindred it is impossible to sort things out among so much information.<br /> <br /> At this point I'd say that absolutely everything about the kindred, with every detail, is accessible to the general public, just buried in the sea of weirdness and pop-culture and mixed with a shitton of false information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T17:57:07-07:00","id":1465580,"title":"","content":"My personal take is that leaking the basics to the public under the guise of fiction (including rpgs) actually reinforces the Masquerade because it makes anyone who does try to go public look like someone who can\u2019t tell real life from some popular work of fiction.<br /> <br /> Basically, someone claiming vampires are real in such a situation looks like some nut who unironically lists their religion as \u201cJedi.\u201d<br /> <br /> In my own setting \u201cKindred the Embraced\u201d was an effort by some neonates who were executed for what was seen as an egregious Masquerade breach (which is why it lasted only 8 episodes) and their claims of doing it for pretty much the reasons above only recognized in hindsight. \u201cBloodlines\u201d was a more deliberate effort launched by a group of Anarchs to basically make unusual activity in the Free States be blown off as nutters who can\u2019t tell video games from real life (though it only became a cult classic).<br /> <br /> This goes basically in line with my Order of Hermes once using an Ars Magica LARP as cover for one of their conclaves. There\u2019s just something to be said for taking refuge in audacity and being a vampire LARPing as a vampire at a vampire-themed nightclub that also sells chincy jewelry based on the \u201cclan logos.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T18:19:10-07:00","id":1465584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465564-in-setting-vampire-texts-and-the-general-public?p=1465580#post1465580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal take is that leaking the basics to the public under the guise of fiction (including rpgs) actually reinforces the Masquerade because it makes anyone who does try to go public look like someone who can\u2019t tell real life from some popular work of fiction.<br /> <br /> Basically, someone claiming vampires are real in such a situation looks like some nut who unironically lists their religion as \u201cJedi.\u201d<br /> <br /> In my own setting \u201cKindred the Embraced\u201d was an effort by some neonates who were executed for what was seen as an egregious Masquerade breach (which is why it lasted only 8 episodes) and their claims of doing it for pretty much the reasons above only recognized in hindsight. \u201cBloodlines\u201d was a more deliberate effort launched by a group of Anarchs to basically make unusual activity in the Free States be blown off as nutters who can\u2019t tell video games from real life (though it only became a cult classic).<br /> <br /> This goes basically in line with my Order of Hermes once using an Ars Magica LARP as cover for one of their conclaves. There\u2019s just something to be said for taking refuge in audacity and being a vampire LARPing as a vampire at a vampire-themed nightclub that also sells chincy jewelry based on the \u201cclan logos.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Jedi religion is actually a thing and, despite drawing iconography from Star Wars, they don't really believe they'll become telekinetic space paladins or anything, it's a metaphor.<br /> <br /> This was a very, very poor comparison.<br /> <br /> An as a vampire in a Vampire LARP, I would enjoy myself playing as other clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T18:21:11-07:00","id":1465586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465564-in-setting-vampire-texts-and-the-general-public?p=1465580#post1465580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal take is that leaking the basics to the public under the guise of fiction (including rpgs) actually reinforces the Masquerade because it makes anyone who does try to go public look like someone who can\u2019t tell real life from some popular work of fiction.<br /> <br /> <b>Basically, someone claiming vampires are real in such a situation looks like some nut who unironically lists their religion as \u201cJedi.\u201d</b><br /> <br /> In my own setting \u201cKindred the Embraced\u201d was an effort by some neonates who were executed for what was seen as an egregious Masquerade breach (which is why it lasted only 8 episodes) and their claims of doing it for pretty much the reasons above only recognized in hindsight. \u201cBloodlines\u201d was a more deliberate effort launched by a group of Anarchs to basically make unusual activity in the Free States be blown off as nutters who can\u2019t tell video games from real life (though it only became a cult classic).<br /> <br /> This goes basically in line with my Order of Hermes once using an Ars Magica LARP as cover for one of their conclaves. There\u2019s just something to be said for taking refuge in audacity and being a vampire LARPing as a vampire at a vampire-themed nightclub that also sells chincy jewelry based on the \u201cclan logos.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel insulted.<br /> <br /> Star Wars was a big influence on my spiritual development.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yes, probably not a good idea to call out people's beliefs.<br /> <br /> Fun fact: The Troika website had fiction that said Bloodlines was actually an in-universe video game with Lucita and Vannevar Thomas having an argument over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-27-2021, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T19:07:11-07:00","id":1465593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465564-in-setting-vampire-texts-and-the-general-public?p=1465586#post1465586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Star Wars was a big influence on my spiritual development.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can feel the hate flowing through you...<br /> <br /> (cough)<br /> <br /> In terms of vampire media in the WoD, most of it that the Camarilla can influence will be toothless, if you pardon the pun. Consider something like the <i>Twilight </i>movies as compared to movies like <i>Near Dark</i> or <i>Martin</i>. That is to say, in vampire media the Camarilla can influence will distort the weaknesses and powers of the vampires, and the vampires will be protagonists. They would at least try to put a stop to media like <i>Near Dark</i> (where the vampires are savage monsters) or <i>Martin </i>(where the &quot;vampires&quot; is a rapist and asshole). Vampire media in the WoD is probably pretty dull stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T20:38:11-07:00","id":1465597,"title":"","content":"I disagree. Excessive propaganda is obvious propaganda. If every Vampire-themed media makes them sympathetic it may raise some eye-brows for absolutely no reason.<br /> <br /> The best thing the Camarilla does with Vampire-themed media is not dealing with it. As long as no actual evidence is leaked, every information is harmless if there is no context to distinguish good and bad information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T20:42:47-07:00","id":1465598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465564-in-setting-vampire-texts-and-the-general-public?p=1465597#post1465597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. Excessive propaganda is obvious propaganda. If every Vampire-themed media makes them sympathetic it may raise some eye-brows for absolutely no reason.<br /> <br /> The best thing the Camarilla does with Vampire-themed media is not dealing with it. As long as no actual evidence is leaked, every information is harmless if there is no context to distinguish good and bad information.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine there's differences of opinion on how to handle it.<br /> <br /> * Toreador will very much love to support the idea of vampires as dark, tragic, romantic antiheroes that everyone wants to be.<br /> * Tremere will want to get rid of vampires as a legend and would love for them to be forgotten completely.<br /> * Ventrue would see the vast amount of $$$ to be made from marketing the legends of the undead even if it is a stupid idea<br /> * You might have Anarchs who believe the Masquerade will eventually fall and a &quot;controlled crash&quot; is the best way to handle it (I.e. NIGHT ROAD's take on it)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T20:59:53-07:00","id":1465599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465564-in-setting-vampire-texts-and-the-general-public?p=1465593#post1465593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can feel the hate flowing through you...<br /> <br /> (cough)<br /> <br /> In terms of vampire media in the WoD, most of it that the Camarilla can influence will be toothless, if you pardon the pun. Consider something like the <i>Twilight </i>movies as compared to movies like <i>Near Dark</i> or <i>Martin</i>. That is to say, in vampire media the Camarilla can influence will distort the weaknesses and powers of the vampires, and the vampires will be protagonists. They would at least try to put a stop to media like <i>Near Dark</i> (where the vampires are savage monsters) or <i>Martin </i>(where the &quot;vampires&quot; is a rapist and asshole). Vampire media in the WoD is probably pretty dull stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not exactly. Medieval and renaissance theatre could get away with a lot of violence, sex &amp; more, as long as, in following with the religiously-influenced thought of the times, the parts responsible paid for their sins in the end and the moral expected from christian values was asserted. Similar logic could definitely run for issues that resonate with the Beast or Humanity for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T21:16:14-07:00","id":1465600,"title":"","content":"While discussing popular vampire literature in the setting is certainly part of this, I am actually more interested in whether things like whether the Guarded Rubrics is known to the British Museum, is the Sargon Fragment occupying a place similar to the Necronomicon in Lovecraft's tales, and if real occultists study the Veneficorum Artus Sanguis written by Etrius. What things could mortals name drop in appropriate circles, and what kind of people should or should not know about them?<br /> <br /> Fictional equivalents to Twilight, Lost Boys, Anne Rice, and other pop vampire literature is fun, but can only add so much to the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T01:34:57-07:00","id":1465613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465564-in-setting-vampire-texts-and-the-general-public?p=1465600#post1465600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While discussing popular vampire literature in the setting is certainly part of this, I am actually more interested in whether things like whether the Guarded Rubrics is known to the British Museum, is the Sargon Fragment occupying a place similar to the Necronomicon in Lovecraft's tales, and if real occultists study the Veneficorum Artus Sanguis written by Etrius. What things could mortals name drop in appropriate circles, and what kind of people should or should not know about them?<br /> <br /> Fictional equivalents to Twilight, Lost Boys, Anne Rice, and other pop vampire literature is fun, but can only add so much to the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>My take on the subject is that the Book of Nod and other vampire relics are things the Camarilla has done their best to scrub out of the hands of mortals. I also fully believe that Anarchs have probably put them up on Amazon and there's no way to remove them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T05:12:57-07:00","id":1465622,"title":"","content":"By my part I already covered &quot;real&quot; texts.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465564-in-setting-vampire-texts-and-the-general-public?p=1465578#post1465578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think unless there is a successful effort in tracking down and securing every single copy of a book, you can bet there's a huge chance a given text went public. And there are others, as the opening letters from 1st and 2nd cores, very recent and very thorough expositions on the Kindred.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> But all said and done, it is hard to tell what the effects are in the public. Without records of any original fragments to give it academic credentials, <i>The Book of Nod</i> is left weightless, the same goes for the <i>Revelations</i>. Saying that your weird book is non-fiction don't really get you much farther than the usual nutjobs that would believe it even if you said it was fiction. The market is choke-full of books about vampires, each with its own version of them, and without knowledge of actual Kindred it is impossible to sort things out among so much information.<br /> <br /> At this point I'd say that absolutely everything about the kindred, with every detail, is accessible to the general public, just buried in the sea of weirdness and pop-culture and mixed with a shitton of false information.</div> </div> </div> </div>I study occultism, I've seen how much stuff is out there. And contrary to some depictions, the &quot;good stuff&quot; however you define it isn't hidden in a forgotten library or behind weird cryptography. It is just hard to sort out.<br /> <br /> You want to summon demons to do your bidding? The Lesser Key of Solomon is literally a 5 minutes search to download, and with reputable sources for you to confirm it is really the medieval text. You want to find the &quot;true Solomon's text unwarped&quot;? Tough luck, if that thing exists you not only will find it in the internet, you'll also find literally thousands of very serious texts claiming to be the real deal, each one with either too complex or too shady a history behind the source.<br /> <br /> Can you piece together some reliable source to figure out how to recognize the truth? Well, if you dive on the sea of thrash and read everything there, maybe. The more you know what you're looking for, the &quot;easier&quot; it gets, but if it was easy we would live in a very different world.<br /> <br /> And that is regardless, again, of what you call the &quot;good stuff&quot;, if you really thinks you can summon spirits, if you want to sort out the history of the writing of the Lesser Key, if you want to identify true authorship of some particular copy or hoax. The reasons behind occult research are manifold even in a world where vampires don't exist, imagine in a world where they do.<br /> <br /> Unless a specific book had every single copy tightly controlled, it is likely out there, publicly known in digital format, by now probably with good formatting, clearly visible, inbuilt audio translation and digital bookmarks, available for download on many websites and good cloud storage sites, right at the side of the &quot;true&quot; account of someone's astral journey to the Empire of Cats in the moon during a trip of magic mushrooms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T06:25:27-07:00","id":1465636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465564-in-setting-vampire-texts-and-the-general-public?p=1465622#post1465622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By my part I already covered &quot;real&quot; texts.<br /> <br /> I study occultism, I've seen how much stuff is out there. And contrary to some depictions, the &quot;good stuff&quot; however you define it isn't hidden in a forgotten library or behind weird cryptography. It is just hard to sort out.<br /> <br /> You want to summon demons to do your bidding? The Lesser Key of Solomon is literally a 5 minutes search to download, and with reputable sources for you to confirm it is really the medieval text. You want to find the &quot;true Solomon's text unwarped&quot;? Tough luck, if that thing exists you not only will find it in the internet, you'll also find literally thousands of very serious texts claiming to be the real deal, each one with either too complex or too shady a history behind the source.<br /> <br /> Can you piece together some reliable source to figure out how to recognize the truth? Well, if you dive on the sea of thrash and read everything there, maybe. The more you know what you're looking for, the &quot;easier&quot; it gets, but if it was easy we would live in a very different world.<br /> <br /> And that is regardless, again, of what you call the &quot;good stuff&quot;, if you really thinks you can summon spirits, if you want to sort out the history of the writing of the Lesser Key, if you want to identify true authorship of some particular copy or hoax. The reasons behind occult research are manifold even in a world where vampires don't exist, imagine in a world where they do.<br /> <br /> Unless a specific book had every single copy tightly controlled, it is likely out there, publicly known in digital format, by now probably with good formatting, clearly visible, inbuilt audio translation and digital bookmarks, available for download on many websites and good cloud storage sites, right at the side of the &quot;true&quot; account of someone's astral journey to the Empire of Cats in the moon during a trip of magic mushrooms.</div> </div> </div> </div>H.P. Lovecraft notably had the Necronomicon not hidden away under lock and key but available in Miskatonic University's archives, which was not an occult university but just an Ivy League school's archives. The implication being that it was something that any reputable scholar could journey down to the place to ask to check out, put on some plastic gloves, and go through as long as they promised not to damage it.<br /> <br /> But I, interestingly, handle Kindred Mythology a bit differently in my games. THE BOOK OF NOD, ERICYNE FRAGMENTS, REVELATIONS OF THE DARK MOTHER and so on aren't treated as the Kindred Bibles. Well, possibly by the Sabbat and virtually every Pack has a copy printed out for them, but Bulfinch's Mythology. The Book of Nod as it is known among vampires was assembled by Aristotle De Laurent relatively recently and is basically a bunch of Kindred folktales. It's not something that was an organized codex of Kindred stories until very recently and was pretty much passed down orally before.<br /> <br /> Indeed, Aristotle's actions in assembling it is something that got enormous numbers of people pissed off at him as, &quot;Caine is our Dark Father&quot; is something that previously was just ONE interpretation of what was effectively united by his actions. Previously, there was the always popular Church of Caine but his &quot;King James version&quot; of the Book of Nod effectively standardized the stories and ideology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T10:51:02-07:00","id":1465671,"title":"","content":"There is something amusing about the idea of &quot;sacred vampire texts&quot; just being available on the internet, either as digital documents or something &quot;original&quot; that can be purchased on Amazon or Ebay. There should be a lot of plot hooks in that as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T13:31:24-07:00","id":1465688,"title":"","content":"I think a major difference between vampire texts and historical works is that all of the historical works were meant to be published and disseminated. So it's entirely possible lots of vampire texts have never been released to the general public. For example, it is entirely conceivable that Etrius' Veneficorum Artus Sanguis is only found in Tremere chantries (and possibly a few other places like a copy possessed by an Arcanum chapterhouse, one held by the Uktena who stole it, a third in the archives of the Society of St Leopold, etc.) and isn't in circulation.<br /> <br /> I've had it as part of my chronicle setting that there are in fact Archons whose main responsibility is to find books that reveal too much about vampires and remove them from circulation (or at least remove the specific parts of them that they care about). They were most active in the first two centuries of the Camarilla pillaging abandoned monasteries, private libraries, and various archives, but the work still goes on today. That sole copy of a chronicle that is the only source of history regarding the Merovingian Dynasty between 604 and 650 is actually a copy whose mentions of vampire involvement was excised by some Toreador archon before they let a human scholar discover the work.<br /> <br /> I do think that various bits of the Book of Nod, Lilith Cycle, etc. probably has been part of the academic scholarship for a while. But they may not be organized as such, and interpreted it as various things. Maybe this piece might be believed to be part of biblical apocrypha like the Book of Enoch. This other piece considered to be a Gnostic text. This other thing a medieval heretic text. This other one a forgery. Cainite scholars may recognize them for what they are, but to mortal academia they might be odd text fragment found in the ruins of a monastery in Turkey and stored in the archives of the Vatican Library.<br /> <br /> But what I think is fun is deciding what things are actually just known to the public, even if is limited to specialists or fringe groups. It might be cool if Egyptologists know the Book of Going Forth by Night just as well as they do the Book of the Dead (aka Book of Going Forth by Day) and other funerary texts. Or that the Codex of the Damned is just one of the many Aztec codices that the Spanish created after the Conquest of Mexico and is just as well known as the Codex Borgia or Florentine Codex. Or that a near intact text of the Cycle of Lilith was discovered by some fictional equivalent to Margaret Murray or Charles Godfrey Leland, and chunks of it is now part of neopaganism because it isn't clear it is talking about vampirism, just Bahari religion on Lilith. This kind of stuff can often lead to hooks by the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T14:11:49-07:00","id":1465694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465564-in-setting-vampire-texts-and-the-general-public?p=1465636#post1465636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> H.P. Lovecraft notably had the Necronomicon not hidden away under lock and key but available in Miskatonic University's archives, which was not an occult university but just an Ivy League school's archives. The implication being that it was something that any reputable scholar could journey down to the place to ask to check out, put on some plastic gloves, and go through as long as they promised not to damage it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but Miskatonic was supposedly one of five educational institutions in the entire world with a copy, along with several others that had been privately owned by occultists and their heirs. It wasn't widely known or readily available like that free U2 album on iTunes. Of course, since John Dee was the scholar who translated the Necronomicon into English, he may have had considerably more time to transcribe additional copies after becoming a Tremere vampire in the WoD...<br /> <br /> I'm not sure which edition it belonged to, but I distinctly recall it being a point that the publication and popularization of <i>Dracula</i> was engineered by Vlad III himself as a smokescreen. A book that at first glance appeared to destroy the Masquerade instead became the single strongest pillar supporting it as its enshrinement into popular culture meant that anyone in Western Civilization who claimed vampires were real would be seen as delusional and confusing fiction with fact.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T14:21:41-07:00","id":1465695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465564-in-setting-vampire-texts-and-the-general-public?p=1465688#post1465688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a major difference between vampire texts and historical works is that all of the historical works were meant to be published and disseminated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually not necessarily. Many books in the past were guarded for one reason or another, and the difficulty in copying them added to the problem.<br /> <br /> But ultimately we're not talking about books from the past <i>in the past</i>. The modern forms of those books are exactly that, modern, compiled by scholars all the same and with mostly the same tools and techniques despite being vampires.<br /> <br /> That's why I think those texts are public. A single scan or transcript, even if incomplete, hitting the internet is enough. Once the thing is in the net, what will those Archons do? By the way, they're a nice idea that I do think make sense, congrats.<br /> <br /> Each person that knows one of those books may put what they know in the web. Anyone with access to a copy can scan or transcribe it. <i>Nosferatu</i> was almost completely destroyed by a judicial decision for being plagiarism on the original <i>Dracula</i>, yet it became an astounding cult success that informs the Vampire genre to this day due to <b>a single </b>copy that survived (the accompanying soundtrack was lost).<br /> <br /> It is particularly good to do so from an academic standpoint. Scientists work better by sharing information so everyone can pass on ideas, and many Kindred working on those texts are scientists. If a Tremere text is copied enough for each two chantries to have a copy, how much time until one gets scanned? What about texts that are common knowledge among the Kindred?<br /> <br /> On my view there are, indeed, books that aren't publicly known, but that requires that every copy be accounted for. Either a copy is lost somewhere and so no one scanned it (it happens even in a library), or it is locked and access to it tightly controlled. The more copies, the harder to keep everything under lock and key. Any copy unaccounted for is a matter of time (a random amount of time) to become public.<br /> <br /> Finally, given how little most of those scholars actually know of the past directly, I think that just as fun as to think that mortal scholars may have access to Kindred-related texts and know nothing of what they really mean, the Kindred may also have a lot of wrong conclusions and not actually know as much about those texts as they pretend to.<br /> <br /> Does the Book of Nod have all the pieces in place? Is every fragment really about the Kindred, or from the same book? Is there some key piece lost in some library, known to a working archaeologist who know nothing about the Kindred, yet understands the text better than any of them? Such is the cost of not sharing information, after all. The pieced text may be very good, but as the work of a single person, it can also be very wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T14:27:10-07:00","id":1465696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465564-in-setting-vampire-texts-and-the-general-public?p=1465694#post1465694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but Miskatonic was supposedly one of five educational institutions in the entire world with a copy, along with several others that had been privately owned by occultists and their heirs. It wasn't widely known or readily available like that free U2 album on iTunes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because Lovecraft wrote about it in the 1920's.<br /> <br /> For an ancient text in that time, it was <b><i>really</i></b> well known in his fiction, most people heard about it and a few transcriptions existed.<br /> <br /> The only reason it wasn't more copied was because, again, it was in the 1920's and it would require a lot of handling to copy, endangering the fragile book.<br /> <br /> Similar texts IRL were handled similarly at the time, but nowadays would be scanned from afar with proper technology to capture the images without endangering the original, and the entire book would be on the internet. As, again, already happened to a lot of similarly old texts recovered IRL.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T16:37:28-07:00","id":1465714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465564-in-setting-vampire-texts-and-the-general-public?p=1465694#post1465694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, since John Dee was the scholar who translated the Necronomicon into English, he may have had considerably more time to transcribe additional copies after becoming a Tremere vampire in the WoD...</div> </div> </div> </div>That reminds me that technically the Necronomicon does exist in the World of Darkness. In the first Tremere Clanbook, it's mentioned as the Al-Azif (written by Abd Al-Azrad) in the section discussing the Order of the Wyrm within the Tremere. Lovecraft himself said Al-Azif was the original title in Arabic in his History of the Necronomicon, and Chaosium had popularized the idea that &quot;Abd al-Azrad&quot; was the true Arabic name of Abdul Alhazred.<br /> <br /> It's not quite clear if they really mean the Necronomicon and the Cthulhu Mythos are part of the World of Darkness because this version of the book seems to reference the Wyrm and its author was a vampire. Not Lovecraftian concepts at all. It's likely the authors just having some fun, and we shouldn't take the easter egg seriously.<br /> <br /> In my chronicles, I use the Liber Labyrinthus (a Nephandic text in Mage) in the same kind of role as the Necronomicon does in Cthulhu games, so I'd just swap that in for book used by the Order of the Wyrm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T17:00:02-07:00","id":1465717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465564-in-setting-vampire-texts-and-the-general-public?p=1465696#post1465696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For an ancient text in that time, it was <b><i>really</i></b> well known in his fiction, most people heard about it and a few transcriptions existed.</div> </div> </div> </div> We should keep in mind that Lovecraft's protagonists aren't exactly regular people. They tend to be antiquarians or occult experts. Lovecraft tends to name drop the Necronomicon at the same times as he mentions real world texts like Turba Philosophorum, Saducismus Triumphatus,<span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">and </span></span></span>Daemonolatreiae libri tres. The Necronomicon is probably just as well known as those books. In other words, it isn't well known at all outside a very specific subset of people. And even those probably just know of it by its reputation and a few quotes, not having actually read it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T18:11:40-07:00","id":1465727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465564-in-setting-vampire-texts-and-the-general-public?p=1465717#post1465717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We should keep in mind that Lovecraft's protagonists aren't exactly regular people. They tend to be antiquarians or occult experts. Lovecraft tends to name drop the Necronomicon at the same times as he mentions real world texts like Turba Philosophorum, Saducismus Triumphatus,<span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">and </span></span></span>Daemonolatreiae libri tres. The Necronomicon is probably just as well known as those books. In other words, it isn't well known at all outside a very specific subset of people. And even those probably just know of it by its reputation and a few quotes, not having actually read it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is still known, and again, known in the 20's. The characters also aren't that unusual: they're archaeologists and antiquarians, but by their monologues we also get that the Necronomicon is well known within the field.<br /> <br /> Not a popular knowledge? Sure. But reasonably common in academic circles, not unlike, lets say, Vampire: the Requiem among RPG players, maybe more. And that in a time that actually most people never read it since there was only 5 copies and the whole thing with Miskatonic was to have the most complete copy.<br /> <br /> Would the same stories happen today, the book would be already on the internet for a long time, as are books similarly old and arcane, like the Voynich Manuscript.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T18:49:06-07:00","id":1465737,"title":"","content":"Black Fox, in addition to that, the Necronomicon is featured in <i>The Red Sign</i>. Though it really seems to be the Necronomicon Ex Mortis of <i>Evil Dead</i> fame rather than Lovecraft's conception of the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T06:09:51-07:00","id":1465759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465564-in-setting-vampire-texts-and-the-general-public?p=1465737#post1465737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Black Fox, in addition to that, the Necronomicon is featured in <i>The Red Sign</i>. Though it really seems to be the Necronomicon Ex Mortis of <i>Evil Dead</i> fame rather than Lovecraft's conception of the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>For pop culture purposes there's little difference between the two. Even in Lovecraft many physical aspects of the book are unsettling and it does have strange powers.<br /> <br /> Of course, it is because of the information therein and not because the book is magical, exactly, but on pop culture translation the distinction get lost easily, so the <i>Ex Mortis</i> isn't the only instance of that kind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T14:57:30-07:00","id":1465835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465564-in-setting-vampire-texts-and-the-general-public?p=1465688#post1465688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think that various bits of the Book of Nod, Lilith Cycle, etc. probably has been part of the academic scholarship for a while. But they may not be organized as such, and interpreted it as various things. Maybe this piece might be believed to be part of biblical apocrypha like the Book of Enoch. This other piece considered to be a Gnostic text. This other thing a medieval heretic text. This other one a forgery. Cainite scholars may recognize them for what they are, but to mortal academia they might be odd text fragment found in the ruins of a monastery in Turkey and stored in the archives of the Vatican Library.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth noting in this too is that it\u2019s not like Cain was \u201cCaine\u2019s\u201d actual given name, any more than Adam was really called Adam (which in Hebrew just means Man) or Eve called Eve or Abel actually called Abel. It\u2019s translations of translations that, if actually true, are written down from oral histories thousands of years (with all the associated linguistic drift) after the events occurred.<br /> <br /> The Book of Nod and the associated works were compiled and translated from fragments\u2026 which probably means in one fragment it\u2019s Akkadian and is referring to some immortal blood god-king or father of night by a fitting Akkadian name and due to various cues the text compiler decides it is a reference and translated that name as \u201cCaine.\u201d<br /> <br /> Basically, take each separate sub-section (or set of events in a longer narrative) of the Book of Nod, make each a separate document with different names for all the figures in that fragment\u2026 and that is what the mortals have; a bunch of unconnected fragments of folklore from dozens of cultures spanning thousands of years.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s all there, but only someone who\u2019s literally spent centuries trying to study the material would ever be able to compile it into a single connected narrative (and only in line with their personal theories and biases\u2026 they could have absolutely thrown out a key fragments that were actually true just because it didn\u2019t fit with their own conclusions of what it should look like\u2026 and suddenly some unrelated nomad whose name was pronounced like the English word \u201cKeen\u201d or \u201cQin\u201d who was cursed by some blood spirit* gets conflated by the scholar with the biblical Cain (because no one in history has ever had the same name**, much less just a similar sounding one) and Lilith.<br /> <br /> * And to top it off this story fragment isn\u2019t even about the first vampire, but an early fomori.<br /> <br /> ** Person 1: \u201cI bet you can\u2019t name 23 popes.\u201d<br /> Person 2: \u201cJohn.\u201d<br /> Person 1: [beat] \u201cDammit, that\u2019s not fair.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T16:03:17-07:00","id":1465842,"title":"","content":"First of all, I'm definitely asking a Bubastis if the Heavyside Layer is real if I ever meet one.<br /> <br /> Second, and perhaps pertinent to the discussion because Caine is an important figure in it: Days of Fire, the chapbook for D:tF, is presented as an English translation for public distribution of a Latin version (kept at Oxford) and an older Greek version (kept at Yale).<br /> <br /> As the fictional publisher character points out in the preface, the new translation was rushed to press in response to the murder of the translator by an unknown killer - who turns out to be Lucifer, the original author. A short fiction published later suggests that the killing was done to draw attention to the text, delivering Lucifer's prophecies about the coming end of the world out to humankind as a warning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T17:46:24-07:00","id":1465850,"title":"","content":"Two things occur;<br /> <br /> A - Each to their own, and so do whatever works in your own game.<br /> <br /> B - For my games Caine, Lilith, the second and third generations had nothing to do with any of text they are purported to have written. They were all composed centuries and millennia after the supposed writers were active. Mostly they were written by people who never met Caine, Lilith, the second and third generation. Sometimes these were written by true believers, sometimes they were written by con-artists. This goes for most such texts.<br /> <br /> That said, I think these texts are probably available in some form on the internet in either digital form or available for purchase. Which strikes me as funny. And at least some of the Camarilla try to chase these instances down, which is like playing a forever game of wack-a-mole. But they can't control everything, so some slips through their fingers to end up among the living.<br /> <br /> Also, I suspect some of the vampires display their bits of ancient texts like the ones in Blade, so the Prince or whomever can show off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5KEPNZMpME0\" data-code=\"5KEPNZMpME0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/5KEPNZMpME0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> The vampire owning the display would be cranky if people got into a fight in his prize room.<br /> <br /> The book <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dark_Colony\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Dark Colony</i></a> also has the book, the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Madeline_Coventry\" target=\"_blank\">Ur Codex</a>, which seems to be a variation on the &quot;forbidden book of knowledge which is forbidden.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 10-29-2021, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T17:59:45-07:00","id":1465853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465564-in-setting-vampire-texts-and-the-general-public?p=1465835#post1465835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, take each separate sub-section (or set of events in a longer narrative) of the Book of Nod, make each a separate document with different names for all the figures in that fragment\u2026 and that is what the mortals have; a bunch of unconnected fragments of folklore from dozens of cultures spanning thousands of years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably each piece of text is actually more than one document, as the scholar compared several fragments he thought to be similar enough. It is also a translation, so he is comparing many pieces in many languages and with many version differences, trying to make sense of them, then translating them to English with his own opinion on what they really should look like.<br /> <br /> All that, obviously, isn't being peer-reviewed and no reference is given to the original sources, so no one can verify his process in any significant way. Very bad science it is, Becket is a far better scholar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}